# Included or NotBefore in CCADB's public report IncludedCACertificateReportForMSFTCSV --
# that Debian's ca-certificates lacks. Each certificate is crt.sh's, checked against CCADB's
# SHA-256. sg-roots (src/sg-roots.c) puts them into the machine's Root store marked with the
# uses given ("# uses:"), which wine-sg 7602 honours: none is trusted for a web server.
# NotBefore roots (Symantec's, distrusted for new certificates) are kept for the signatures
# made before; their cut-off dates are not in the report. Disabled roots are left out.
